    "systems"
  ],
  "slug": "flow-matching-continuous-molecular-a38a",
  "summary": "New preprints combine zero-shot, in-context and pretrained response prediction with inference of the regulatory paths and pathways perturbations act through.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is predicting single-cell transcriptional responses to perturbation and attributing them to regulatory structure. On the prediction side, CytoWave uses perturbation-centric two-stage pretraining across datasets. RELAY conditions on measured control–perturbed pairs via relational in-context learning. SPEAR applies flow-based generation with spectral Laplacian gene encodings. EMBER probes frozen contextualized gene embeddings for single, digenic and drug responses. GRAFT transfers genetic perturbation information to zero-shot drug-response prediction across cell types. Mechanistic work includes REGA-perturb, which resolves TF–regulatory element–gene paths from Perturb-seq latent programs and reference epigenomes, and RAPTORGraph, a beta-VAE with a graph pathway encoder for causal discovery. ExPert inverts the problem, inferring causal perturbations from observed states across 12 contexts. Adjacent work covers regulator prioritization for reprogramming transitions (FateDriver), gene-set selection for GRN inference (GSET), context-dependent network rewiring via sparse ODEs (Co2ODE), and age-indexed gene sets (MAGE). What is new is coupling cross-context or cross-modality generalization with explicit regulatory, pathway or dynamical constraints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
